      "id": "M4112-A",
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "prompt": "A. A fictional industrial classifier trains a shared encoder using a supervised class loss plus two auxiliary losses. One auxiliary loss pairs an earlier context in one augmented view with a later encoded feature from the same sample in another view; other samples in the batch provide negative pairs. The other builds a sample-to-sample similarity target from the classifier's estimated class distributions and fits contextual similarities to it. At test time only the encoder and classifier run. The draft says: 'A temporal forecasting module detects future faults. A pseudo-label graph then learns physical process connections and fuses them with features for deployment.' Provide two or three connected English abstract-method sentences and a brief Chinese explanation of any needed corrections. No results or novelty comparison are supplied.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Describe actual training interactions and test-time diagnostic output without fictitious module sequence.",
        "Retain sample-level estimated class guidance and latent temporal pairing."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Claim physical forecasting, process topology or negative-pair fault labels.",
        "Invent empirical improvement or novelty."
      ],
      "outcome": "pass",
      "evaluator": "Maintainer semantic review; no independent second grader",
      "response_trace": "responses/v4112-revised.md",
      "review_trace": "reviews/v4112-independent-evaluation.md",
      "evaluation_phase": "fresh_context_frozen_candidate",
