    {
      "id": "M4112-C",
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "prompt": "C. Two published engineering-journal papers define ordinary contrastive learning, while a third proposes its own component named Age-Calibrated Contrastive Gate. A curator wants the complete latter name in the shared terminology bank and translates it as 年龄门控 from a machine-translation suggestion. The only Chinese search result available is an inaccessible page's snippet. Explain in Chinese which entries can be recommended, what remains to check, and whether the third paper's exact component name may still be used when reviewing that paper. Do not browse or fabricate additional references.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Separate paired base-name evidence from the full paper-specific name.",
        "Keep Chinese verification incomplete and preserve attributed source names."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Treat partial names or snippets as sufficient complete-name/translation evidence.",
        "Forbid attribution of a genuine source-specific component."
