    {
      "id": "M4112-D",
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "prompt": "D. A fictional quality-monitoring study classifies defects whose signatures may include amplitude changes. It proposes multiplying all unlabeled signal amplitudes by random factors, using the weak-view classifier's argmax as a target for a strong view, and adding a consistency loss. Its three draft contributions are 'a CNN', 'a pseudo-label module', and 'invariance to all production fluctuations'. No nearest-prior comparison, augmentation check or new result is available. Discuss in Chinese how to improve the contribution framing without inventing evidence, and give one concise provisional English contribution sentence based only on the implemented relation.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Link generated targets, training view and consistency objective.",
        "Separate a provisional mechanism description from demonstrated novelty and amplitude invariance."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Certify physical invariance, pseudo-label accuracy or three independent novelties.",
        "Demand a universal ban on augmentation or invent performance."
